course: dictionary
lesson: 12887
title: Trapped or tricked?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Entrap is a verb, so it is a doing word. To entrap something is to catch it in a trap, so it cannot get away. «The mouse was entrapped under the wooden box.» The mouse could not get out, so entrapped means caught.
explain: Entrap can also mean to trick someone into doing something wrong, so they can be caught. «The villain entrapped the knight with a fake letter.» The letter was a trick, and the knight was led into danger. Look for clues like trap, trick or catch.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping in an easy word. If «trapped» or «tricked» fits the sentence and makes sense, you have found the meaning.
fact: Entrap means to catch someone or something in a trap, or to trick someone into doing something wrong.
fact: «Entrapped» is the past tense, and «entraps» and «entrapping» are other forms of the same word.
fact: «Entrapment» is a noun. In law, it means police unfairly trick someone into committing a crime.
fact: «The sailors were entrapped by the ice» means the ice trapped them so they could not move.
fact: «The spider entraps flies in its sticky web» shows an animal catching its food in a trap.
exercise: «The mouse was entrapped under the wooden box.» What does entrapped mean? | Fed and happy | *Caught in a trap, unable to get out | Painted bright red | Set free and running away
exercise: «The villain entrapped the knight with a fake letter.» What does entrapped suggest? | Rescued from the rain | Woken up early by a loud noise | *Tricked into doing something dangerous | Given a lovely gift
exercise: Find and copy the one word in «The spider entraps flies in its sticky web» that means catches in a trap. | sticky | *entraps | flies | web
test: «The fox entrapped the hen in the barn.» What is the best meaning of entrapped here? | Lost on the way | Taught to dance | Sung to sleep | Given a meal | *Caught in a trap
test: Which word means tricked into doing something wrong, so that you can be caught? | Entertain | *Entrap | Embrace | Enjoy
exam: «The police were accused of entrapment after they tricked the man into a crime.» What does entrapment mean here? | A friendly party with games | A very loud noise | A long, peaceful rest | *Unfair tricking of someone into committing a crime
